# Target C: the one-deficit population is excluded for all small M=4 wall curvatures

Date: 2026-10-07. Base `88f38a9c`; main
`dcc21aa879b61662318bceb9aeb174792e074eb0`; state
`2026-10-06.audit.71`. **Proved candidate awaiting independent audit.**
No canonical promotion, arbitrary-M assertion, macroscopic extraction or
Level I closure is claimed.

## 1. Quantified theorem and exact consequence

There exists theta_0>0 such that, for every 0<theta<theta_0, the specified
six-direction curved unit wall with M=4 admits a strict packet of N=37
sites after deleting wall vertex (1,3). Thus an arbitrary canonical old
source with z=N-1=36 interior points in this wall is impossible. More
generally the same packet pays every z<=36 by selecting z+1 sites.

`all-small-curvature strict N-site packet -> replace every old interior
label and one actual wall vertex -> zero new contacts, at least two old
wall contacts lost -> audit.64 full-source contradiction`.

This theorem does not classify any old cloud. In particular no missing
lattice-site hypothesis is imposed on the source. It directly spends the
one-deficit population which the inherited N-1-site packet could not pay.
The auxiliary vacancy belongs only to the newly constructed packet.

## 2. Rational-function opening certificate

Use t=tan(theta/2) and the descending-order sorting geometry. Its complex
unit factors are

`z_h=((1-t^2)+2it)/(1+t^2)` raised to `3-2h`, h=0,1,2,3.

In a sector, set S_r=sum_(h<r) z_h and

`p_(r,j)=S_(r-j) u+(S_r-S_(r-j)) v`, 0<=j<=r<=4,

then rotate by multiples of pi/3. The radius-four sites are precisely the
old curved wall. Delete target site h=(1,2), leaving 36 interior sites.

Each site is a linear combination of the four independent complex
symbols z_h with unit triangular-direction coefficients. A difference
with exactly one nonzero unit coefficient has *exactly* unit length,
since |z_h|=1. The supplied verifier checks this coefficient identity
for all actual unit pairs. It also verifies positive leading squared-
distance gaps for all 1654 remaining pairs of the full wall-plus-chart
set. Hence no inactive lower pair is omitted: for all sufficiently small
t>0 the complete chart has exactly the specified 92 unit rows incident
to an interior site, and all other such pairs are strictly separated.

Let R(t) contain those 92 moving-coordinate rows. An explicitly stored
73-row basis defines a square system in the 72 velocity coordinates d
and one auxiliary eta. A selected contact row is `(R(t)d)_e-eta=0`;
a selected coordinate row fixes one component of d to +1 or -1.
The basis and right-hand side are supplied in
`research/target_c_one_deficit_opening_basis_M4_2026_10_07.json`.
Its coefficient entries are rational functions in Q(sqrt(3))(t).

The certificate proves that this square matrix has a nonzero determinant:
all 73 exact Laurent elimination pivots have nonzero leading coefficients.
Three pivot valuations are one and all others are zero. Therefore it is
invertible for every sufficiently small t>0 and defines a meromorphic
velocity field d(t).

For *every* one of the 92 rows the exact solution satisfies

`(R(t)d(t))_e = c_e t^(k_e)+O(t^(p_e))`,

with `c_e>0`, `p_e>k_e`. The orders k_e lie in {0,1,2,3,4,5,6}; every
certified remainder order is at least nine. Thus each row is strictly
positive for all sufficiently small t>0. The common onset exists because
there are finitely many rows. No floating sign or sampled onset is used.
In particular some contacts only open through order six in this velocity
certificate. A strict second-order test is not an exhaustive release test.

The certificate uses exact truncated Laurent arithmetic with tracked
absolute remainder orders. If a=O(t^p) plus a known leading part of
valuation v, its inverse is known through order p-2v. For a product the
known order is min(p_a+v_b,p_b+v_a); for a sum it is the minimum input
order. Gaussian elimination and back substitution use these rules. A
pivot or sign is accepted only when a known nonzero coefficient lies
strictly below its certified remainder order. These are identities for
rational functions, not an extrapolation of finite parameter evaluations.

At each fixed small t, all 92 contacts therefore strictly open under
`p -> p+epsilon d(t)` for sufficiently small epsilon>0. All inactive
pairs and interior containment already have strict finite margins, so
they persist upon choosing epsilon smaller. The field need not be affine,
C2 in theta, bounded uniformly in M, or a motion of the old source.

## 3. A universal small-curvature root lemma

The following elementary root calculation is valid for every fixed M>=3
in the same descending-order sorting chart; it requires no opening claim
for general M. Let v be the wall site (1,M-1), omit the interior target
h=(1,M-2), put w=v_basis-u_basis=(-1/2,sqrt(3)/2), and define

`r=exp(i(M-2)theta) w`, `root=v+3 sin(theta) Jr`.

The two incident wall edges have directions exp(i(M-3)theta)w and
exp(i(M-1)theta)w. Direct squaring gives root-to-neighbour distances

`1+3 sin^2(theta)>1`.

At zero, the only other interior unit neighbour of v after omitting h
is a=(0,M-1). Its sorting velocity is (M-1)Jv_basis. The wall site's
velocity is -(M-1)Jw and the root's velocity is (4-M)Jw. Therefore

`(v(0)-a(0)) dot (root'(0)-a'(0))=(sqrt(3)/2)(2M-5)>0`.

All remaining root-to-chart or root-to-wall pairs have a strictly positive
limiting gap, and hence remain above one for small theta. This explicitly
explains why the omitted target site is the relevant blocker; keeping it
would instead give a negative first margin -3sqrt(3)/2.

For containment, consider edge j=0,...,M-1 on the same wall side. Its
limiting tangent is w, first tangent coefficient is (2j-M+1)Jw, and its
initial endpoint velocity is -j(M-j)Jw. Put k=M-1-j. The first signed
cross-product coefficient from that edge to the root is

`4-M+j(M-j)-(2j-M+1)(M-1-j)=k^2-k+3>0`.

All other wall sides have strict limiting containment margins, since
v(0) is in the relative interior of the chosen side. The root is therefore
strictly inside the actual convex wall for every sufficiently small
positive theta. This checks all wall support lines, not just the local
vertex cone.

For M=4, choose epsilon still smaller to preserve all root clearances when
opening the 36 auxiliary sites. The root plus those opened sites is the
required strict 37-site packet. This is a finite feasible endpoint for
*each* small positive theta.

## 4. Complete canonical exchange

Delete all z<=36 old interior points and the old wall vertex v. Assign
all z+1 deleted labels to distinct sites of the 37-site strict packet.
No assumption is made about old interior contacts or coordinates.

Retained-to-retained old constraints do not change. Every new lower pair
inside the packet or to a retained wall vertex is strict. The canonical
one-vertex convex-wall shield then checks every retained exterior point,
including contact isolates. Every inserted point lies strictly inside
the two-dimensional old wall hull, so strict convexity of squared distance
gives strict upper distance below the actual old D to every retained
source point. Packet-packet upper distances are likewise strict. Old
actual diameter pairs are unchanged or removed, and inactive upper
exceptions are not dropped.

Cardinality is unchanged; there are zero new contacts and therefore no
new unit triangle. At least the two old incident wall contacts disappear,
with all old interior contacts counted as further possible losses. Actual
diameter-pair loss is not needed. Audit.64 excludes this triangle-free
replacement by global or contact minimality.

